1
00:00:06,980 --> 00:00:08,208
Hey Connor.

2
00:00:08,920 --> 00:00:10,060
What are you doing this weekend?

3
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:11,060
Hi!

4
00:00:11,540 --> 00:00:12,880
I’m quite busy actually.

5
00:00:13,300 --> 00:00:13,620
Why?

6
00:00:14,220 --> 00:00:17,820
Well, it’s just that we’ve got that History test coming up.

7
00:00:18,320 --> 00:00:20,000
Do you want to study together?

8
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:21,400
That would be great!

9
00:00:22,640 --> 00:00:23,740
But, let me see.

10
00:00:25,080 --> 00:00:27,000
Saturday morning is no good.

11
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:28,420
I’m playing football.

12
00:00:28,880 --> 00:00:31,260
It’s the cup final and I can’t miss that.

13
00:00:31,640 --> 00:00:32,640
Of course not.

14
00:00:33,320 --> 00:00:35,800
OK, so what about Friday night?

15
00:00:37,380 --> 00:00:39,400
I’m sorry. I can’t.

16
00:00:39,520 --> 00:00:39,880
I’m busy.

17
00:00:40,647 --> 00:00:46,820
Dad’s taking me to the sports centre to watch the basketball game, but it doesn’t finish until 10 pm.

18
00:00:47,360 --> 00:00:49,120
Yeah, that’s a bit late.

19
00:00:49,780 --> 00:00:52,200
OK, how about Saturday afternoon.

20
00:00:52,779 --> 00:00:53,260
Any chance?

21
00:00:55,820 --> 00:00:59,300
Saturday afternoon, Saturday afternoon.

22
00:01:00,395 --> 00:01:04,780
It’s my brother’s birthday, so we’re going to the restaurant to celebrate.

23
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:08,580
You know, that new American diner on the high street.

24
00:01:08,980 --> 00:01:11,020
Oh, yeah, I’ve heard it’s very good.

25
00:01:11,740 --> 00:01:14,014
What time do you think you’ll finish there?

26
00:01:14,260 --> 00:01:18,140
Probably about 5 pm, but then I’m meeting Nathan.

27
00:01:18,660 --> 00:01:21,500
We’re going to see the new Spider-Man film at the cinema.

28
00:01:22,260 --> 00:01:23,860
Hey, would you like to come?

29
00:01:24,420 --> 00:01:28,600
Hmmm, Spider-Man – not really my thing.

30
00:01:29,280 --> 00:01:31,080
So thanks but no thanks.

31
00:01:31,940 --> 00:01:34,200
I guess that just leaves Sunday.

32
00:01:34,700 --> 00:01:35,980
Yeah, Sunday.

33
00:01:37,680 --> 00:01:39,320
Hmmmm, that’s a problem, too.

34
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:40,720
Why?

35
00:01:41,300 --> 00:01:46,020
Well, my grandparents are coming over and we’re taking them to that outdoor museum.

36
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:49,420
Oh, the one with all the cool old buildings?

37
00:01:49,880 --> 00:01:50,500
That’s right.

38
00:01:51,020 --> 00:01:53,100
My grandad loves that sort of stuff.

39
00:01:53,100 --> 00:01:58,100
I’d invite you, but I’m really sorry, we haven’t got any room in the car.

40
00:01:58,440 --> 00:02:01,140
I don’t want to see old buildings, Connor.

41
00:02:01,600 --> 00:02:03,340
I want to study for the test.

42
00:02:03,500 --> 00:02:04,772
Yeah, of course.

43
00:02:05,280 --> 00:02:08,760
Sunday evening maybe, but only after 8 pm.

44
00:02:09,180 --> 00:02:15,593
I’ve got a piano lesson from 7 to 8 and we won’t be back from the museum much before 6 pm.

45
00:02:16,360 --> 00:02:18,140
No, that’s too late.

46
00:02:18,740 --> 00:02:20,000
What about next weekend?

47
00:02:20,520 --> 00:02:22,460
I’ve got loads of free time next weekend.

48
00:02:22,460 --> 00:02:23,800
I’d love to!

49
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:26,200
But there’s a problem.

50
00:02:26,700 --> 00:02:27,423
What’s that?

51
00:02:27,860 --> 00:02:29,540
The test is on Monday.

52
00:02:30,120 --> 00:02:31,120
This Monday.

53
00:02:31,620 --> 00:02:32,980
First thing in the morning!
